<head>
    <title>Town Rules</title>
    <link href="style.css" rel="stylesheet" />
</head>

<body>
    {% include "navigation.njk" %}
    <div class="rules">
        <h2>Basic Rules</h2>
        <p>1. <b>Every feeling is welcome here.</b> No resident gets evicted and you all belong to this town.</p>
        <p>2. <b>Be kind to your neighbors.</b> Each resident is someone's real feeling. Speak to them the way you'd
            want
            yours to be spoken to.</p>
        <p>3. <b>This is a town, but not a therapy office.</b> You could feel free to express yourself here. But if a
            feeling gets too heavy to carry alone, please reach out to someone you trust or a professional.</p>
        <h2>Living With Your Residents</h2>
        <p>1. <b>Listen before you send them away.</b> Every emotion is trying to tell you something.</p>
        <p>2. <b>Give them a place to stay, but not making one dominant. A feeling can visit without taking over. Notice
                it,
                name it, and let it sit in its corner of town.</b></p>
        <p>3. <b>Be a gentle.</b> Don't scold yourself for who moved in. Every resident arrived for a reason. </p>
    </div>
</body>

</html>